## Investigation (no workers — done directly by coordinator per redirect)
- Pinned released-vs-done semantics across 5 systems:
  board work-claims (release=verb->unclaimed, done=terminal keeps owner),
  claim-collisions (released+done both "closed" for file holding),
  claim-reputation (claim_released vs claim_completed vs claim_flaked),
  inbox-handoff (released=terminal), handoff envelopes (no released).
- Pinned round-bound retries per route: release REQUIRED (#2088), reassign REQUIRED
  (#2262), appendPullRequest REQUIRED, /update note+state OPT-IN (#2078),
  requestId replay dedup OPT-IN (A4).
- OBSERVED FAILURE reproduced (route-level, real handleWorkClaims, in-memory
  registry): a round-1 `done` retried with no preconditions after release+reclaim
  returns 200 and marks round 2 done. Stale-self-retry class, finish path still open.
- Control: same stale done WITH stale preconditions -> 409 work_claim_conflict.

